1 STARTUP

   What govax does each time it starts:

     1. Mounts the system volume on DUA0:, making it the first time (see
        SYSTEM_VOLUME).
     2. Mounts the containers the --mount and --mount-write options
        name, and the default volume (vax.default.volume.file), on DUA1:
        unless configured otherwise.
     3. Runs SYS$MANAGER:STARTUP.COM from the system volume, at command
        level 1, as a login command procedure.  It defines the system
        logical names, sizes the memory (INITIALIZE/VAX and
        INITIALIZE/MEMORY, from the vax.memory.* settings), loads
        SYS$SYSTEM:DEFAULT.ROM, assembles SYS$SOURCES:KERNEL.ASM and
        starts it, defines TTA0: and NLA0:, and last runs
        SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM.
     4. Installs the page file, with paging on.
     5. Runs vax.startup.procedure, if that names a procedure.
     6. Runs the command on govax's command line and exits, or else
        shows the VAX> prompt.

   Your own startup commands belong in SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:
   govax makes it once and never changes it.  Without a system volume
   (--system-file none, or one that can't be used), govax runs its
   built-in copy of STARTUP.COM instead.  See CONFIGURATION KEYS for the
   settings.
